{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 26 — Interactive visualization: Plotly or Altair\n","Objectives:\n","- Build interactive charts.\n","- Add tooltips, selections, and simple dashboards.\n","- Export HTML."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import plotly.express as px, seaborn as sns\n","df = sns.load_dataset('tips')\n","fig = px.scatter(df, x='total_bill', y='tip', color='time', hover_data=['day','size'])\n","fig.show()\n","fig.write_html('interactive_scatter.html')\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Create an interactive histogram with dynamic bins.\n","2) Save to HTML and open in a browser."]}]}
